  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language commonly used with the Apache HTTP Server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* php: ext-pgsql: PHP: SQL injection via improper backslash escaping (CVE-2026-17543)\n\n* php: PHP: Denial of Service via circular symbolic links in phar archives (CVE-2026-7260)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Rebase PHP to 8.2.33 for CVE-2026-17543 and CVE-2026-7260 in 8.10.z (JIRA:Rocky Linux-223938)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
